   "notes": "wasatch_disclosure_tableab, entirely HANDWRITTEN, 3 pages: page 3 is a SECOND copy of the page-2 sheet used as a continuation, carrying the remaining rows AND both grand TOTAL rows. Cover: ROBERT (BOB) ADAMS, Wasatch County Assessor, Republican, Midway UT; signed 6/18/24; NO reporting-period box checked (matches the module's list of filings that mark none) and neither acknowledgement line initialled. RHODES RULE APPLIED TWICE: (a) p2 row 1's amount glyph is cramped and could read 40.00 or 46.00 — only 40.00 lets the twelve rows reach the filer's printed 7,309.39, so 40.00 wins; (b) p3 row 1's amount reads 5,522.84 or 5,522.89 at 200 dpi — the grand total closes only on 5,522.89 (14,082.28 - 7,309.39 - 1,250.00 = 5,522.89), so .89 wins. Both are recorded with the arithmetic as the authority, not a glyph re-read. ONE ITEM A HUMAN SHOULD LOOK AT: p3 Table A row 1's date. At 1200 dpi the first digit has a flat top and a single descending stroke and does NOT carry the double bowl of this filer's unmistakable '3' on p2, i.e. it reads as a 7 — but 7/27/24 is impossible on a Primary report covering through Jun 13 2024 and signed 6/18/24. No printed figure gates a date, so I have left it BLANK with needs_review rather than pick a reading. DITTO MARKS: p2 Table A rows 2-4 hold a pair of ditto strokes; resolved to the row above (Bob Adams) and noted per the ditto rule. FIELD-SHIFT SCREEN: passed on all four table sections — dates are date-shaped, names name-shaped, and counts match (A: 12 dates/12 names/12 amounts on p2, 2/2/2 on p3; B: 12/12/12 on p2, 4/4/4 on p3). Table A on this variant has no address column, so donor_city/state are blank by form design. The filer is himself the largest single donor group (six self-contributions) — recorded as printed, no inference added."
  }
